## Why This Is Asked
Tests multi-tenant inference, per-tenant SLAs, and practical routing inside an MME while keeping data in a VPC.

## Key Concepts
- SageMaker Multi-Model Endpoint and on-demand loading
- Per-tenant routing and model versioning
- Auto Scaling and canary rollouts by tenant
- Drift detection, validation, data residency

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example: per-request routing to specific model on an MME
const { SageMakerRuntimeClient, InvokeEndpointCommand } = require("@aws-sdk/client-sagemaker-runtime");
const client = new SageMakerRuntimeClient({region:'us-east-1'});
async function infer(endpoint, modelName, payload){
  return await client.send(new InvokeEndpointCommand({
    EndpointName: endpoint,
    ContentType: 'application/json',
    Accept: 'application/json',
    Body: JSON.stringify({ instances: [payload], modelName })
  }));
}
``

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a cost-aware, low-latency multi-model inference with per-language isolation, explainability, and secure data access via PrivateLink. It also probes rollout discipline and drift monitoring in production.

## Key Concepts
- Multi-model SageMaker endpoints with per-language routing
- SageMaker Clarify for real-time feature attributions
- PrivateLink access to private data lake and data residency
- Canary rollouts and drift monitoring for safe production
- Caching for explanations to reduce latency impact

## Code Example
```javascript
// pseudo-CDK snippet outline for endpoint + Clarify integration
const clarifiyConfig = {
  enableExplainability: true,
  caching: true,
};
const endpoint = new sagemaker.CfnEndpoint(this, 'LangEndpoint', {
  // model shard per language
  endpointConfigName: 'LangMultiModelConfig',
  // integration with Clarify
  dataCaptureConfig: clarifiyConfig
});
```

